            <ArticleTitle>[Continuous epidural ropivacaine analgesia in adolescents].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The paper deals with the efficiency of postoperative analgesia after thoracoplasty in 43 adolescents with the funnel chest. Within the first 64-72 postoperative hours, the patients received a continuous epidural infusion of 0.2% ropivacaine solution at a rate of 0.3 ml/kg/hr. Analyses of hemodynamic parameters and the pain scale demonstrated the efficiency of this postoperative analgesia in 74.4% of the adolescents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
